  <!-- author -->


    <div class="container-full-width container--padding">
      <div class="container-md">
        <div class="editor-output leading-text editor-output--responsive-img">
          <p>The group phase of the<a data-router-slot="disabled" href="https://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/standings/#group-phase" target="_blank" title="ehfcl.eurohandball.com" data-anchor="#group-phase" type="external"> EHF Champions League Men 2026/27</a> is heading towards its final stages, with only three game days left after the opening of round 5 on Wednesday night. And while some fates were decided, some tickets for the main round are still up for grabs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

<script async type="text/plain" class="_iub_cs_activate js-consent-script" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
<script async type="text/plain" class="_iub_cs_activate js-consent-script" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://www.instagram.com/embed.js" charset="utf-8"></script>



  <div class="container-full-width container--padding" >
    <div class="content-container container-sm">
      <div class="content-block">
        <div class="editor-output editor-output--responsive-img js-consent-content" data-purposes="3">
          <p>The only team that qualified on Wednesday was Industria Kielce, who had to battle for 60 minutes to overcome HC Kriens-Luzern’s resistance. SAH - Aarhus missed the opportunity to book their main round ticket, losing badly against Dinamo in Bucharest.</p><p>In group A, One Veszprém HC made sure they would take the maximum of points with them into the main round, while RK Partizan AdmiralBet secured their first point in the EHF Champions League Men 2026/27.</p><p>Everything is still open in a couple of groups, such as group B, where HBC Nantes put themselves in a precarious position by losing against Vardar. After their results on Wednesday, a win and a loss, respectively, Aalborg Håndbold and Paris Saint-Germain will battle for the top spot in group C next week.</p><ul><li><p>Veszprém will take four points with them into the main round after their second win of the season against Berlin, 39:35</p></li><li><p>despite only needing a point in round 5, Aarhus did not secure their presence in the main round as they suffered a tough defeat against Dinamo, 37:23</p></li><li><p>already qualified, Paris were defeated in Zagreb, 29:28, while Aalborg are sole leaders in group C after their victory over Celje, 34:30</p></li><li><p>Vardar grabbed their first victory of the season in Nantes, 33:27, while Partizan took their first point, drawing against Porto 33:33</p></li><li><p>Kielce had to wait until the final minutes of their game in Kriens-Luzern, when they clinched a 32:30 result, to become the eighth team qualified for the main round</p></li></ul><p>GROUP A</p><h3><a data-router-slot="disabled" href="https://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/matches/details/202711020101001/OneVeszprémHC-FüchseBerlin/" target="_blank" title="ehfcl.eurohandball.com" type="external">One Veszprém HC (HUN) vs Füchse Berlin (GER) 39:35 (20:13)</a></h3><p>H2H: 5-0-5<br>Top scorers: Dragan Pechmalbec 8/9 (One Veszprém HC); Mathias Gidsel 9/12 (Füchse Berlin)</p><p>One could be sure that Berlin would have some nightmares featuring Emil Nielsen on Wednesday night, after the Danish goalkeeper gave another crazy performance for Veszprém. The hosts did not take a goal for the first five minutes of the game, as Nielsen made seven saves in the opening quarter. As a consequence, his team was already ahead by four after 10 minutes. The situation did not get any better for the visitors when Matthes Langhoff was sent off after hitting Ali Zein in the face in minute 15. As they made the most of every opportunity, Veszprém’s lead increased to nine goals shortly before the break; an advantage that two goals from Berlin’s Mijajlo Marsenić reduced to seven ahead of half-time. Things could not get any worse for Füchse and, luckily for them, they did not. Finally finding some offensive solutions in line players Max Darj and Marsenić, they scored three in a row to come back within three with 15 minutes left to play. Veszprém held tight though, and Nedim Remili proved important in the last 12 minutes, scoring three and delivering two assists. Berlin were never able to make things level and Veszprém enjoyed their fifth victory in as many games this season.</p><p><span class="umb-embed-holder" data-embed-constrain="true" data-embed-height="393" data-embed-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gDkIocNna2I" data-embed-width="700"><iframe width="699" height="393" class="_iub_cs_activate" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://www.youtube.com/embed/gDkIocNna2I?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen="" title="One Veszprém HC vs Füchse Berlin | Highlights | EHF Champions League Men 2026/27"></iframe></span></p>
        </div>


<div class="consent-info js-consent-info" data-purposes="3">
    <div class="consent-info-content">
        <h2>This content is blocked</h2>
        <p>You said no to using cookies or similar tools that help improve your experience. To see this content, you would need to update your <a href="javascript:void(0);" class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link">Privacy Preferences</a>.</p>
        <button class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link" data-accept-purposes="3">
            Update
        </button>
    </div>
</div>      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

<div class="container-full-width container--padding">
    <div class="container">
        <blockquote class="blockquote blockquote--fullwidth" cite="Xavi Pascual">
                <div class="blockquote-img-tag-container">
                    <img class="img-responsive blockquote-image" data-loading="lazy"
                         src="/media/5wlj44dr/20261021_veszprem-berlin_3483.jpg"
                         data-src="/media/5wlj44dr/20261021_veszprem-berlin_3483.jpg"
                         alt="20261021 Veszprem Berlin 3483">
                </div>
            <div class="blockquote-text">
The game wasn’t easy. The F&#252;chse players showed once again that they are true to themselves — they always approach the game with great focus. Berlin played brilliantly, but our performance in the first half was simply outstanding. However, at this level, it’s very difficult to maintain that standard throughout an entire match. Berlin scored more goals in the second half and switched to a seven-against-six attack, which made things more difficult for us defensively as well. But the amount of work we put in during the first half was incredible.            </div>
            <div class="blockquote-author">
                <div class="blockquote-name">Xavi Pascual</div>
                <div class="blockquote-position">Head coach, One Veszpr&#xE9;m HC</div>
            </div>
        </blockquote>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="container-full-width container--padding">
    <div class="container">
        <blockquote class="blockquote blockquote--fullwidth" cite="Nicolej Krickau">
                <div class="blockquote-img-tag-container">
                    <img class="img-responsive blockquote-image" data-loading="lazy"
                         src="/media/mg3ftxkc/20261021_veszprem-berlin_4782.jpg"
                         data-src="/media/mg3ftxkc/20261021_veszprem-berlin_4782.jpg"
                         alt="20261021 Veszprem Berlin 4782">
                </div>
            <div class="blockquote-text">
It was clear that the opening stages proved decisive. Our decision-making at the start, particularly our shot selection against Emil Nielsen, was not good enough, and that shaped the rest of the match. However, I think we did a much better job in the second half, with Mathias helping us stick to our game plan and try to find solutions. Ultimately, we had no answer to Veszpr&#233;m in the opening stages, and the advantage they built was enough to see them through to the final whistle.            </div>
            <div class="blockquote-author">
                <div class="blockquote-name">Nicolej Krickau</div>
                <div class="blockquote-position">Head coach, F&#xFC;chse Berlin</div>
            </div>
        </blockquote>
    </div>
</div>

